WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Mark] So Ruby.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.053
- Yes, sir.

00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:05.840
- [Mark] Ruby. Why don't
we take off the hat?

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.683
- Yes, sir.

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:08.820
(laughs)

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.653
- [Mark] OK, Ruby.

00:00:09.653 --> 00:00:10.486
- Yes, sir.

00:00:10.486 --> 00:00:11.319
- [Mark] Ruby, where
are you from originally?

00:00:11.319 --> 00:00:12.290
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.920
- Orange County, California.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.800
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.480
You grew up with both your parents?

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.173
- Yeah, I grew up with both of my parents.

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:23.830
One was a foster and one was a regular.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.700
- [Mark] So...

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.318
- Not foster.

00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:28.880
My dad, married my mom.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.713
- [Mark] Stepdad.

00:00:29.713 --> 00:00:30.602
My stepdad. Yes.

00:00:30.602 --> 00:00:31.967
- [Mark] Mom and stepdad?

00:00:31.967 --> 00:00:32.800
- Yes.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.804
- [Mark] And how was your childhood?

00:00:33.804 --> 00:00:34.637
- Excellent.

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:35.470
- [Mark] It was good?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.370
- Yes.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.203
- [Mark] What kind of kid
were you in high school?

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.980
- At high school, I played sports

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.351
and I did a lot of academics.

00:00:44.351 --> 00:00:46.620
I graduated six months
early before my class.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.530
- [Mark] You're a good student.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:48.363
Yes, sir.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.450
- [Mark] And then where,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.090
where'd your life go after, after school?

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:52.923
- After school,

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.340
I have friends

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.210
and, um,

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.170
they took me to a whole

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.220
nother place in life.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.780
I met the spaceship man (mumbles).

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.713
And my dad, he's Mexican mafia.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.490
So, um, yeah

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.252
he brought me a lot of
wonders in the world.

00:01:18.252 --> 00:01:19.085
- [Mark] He brought a lot of what?

00:01:19.085 --> 00:01:20.650
- A lot of wonders in the world.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.730
- [Mark] After high
school, you went where?

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:24.680
- After high school

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.073
I went to Apple Valley, California.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.330
After high school, we stayed probably

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.540
about five years after that,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.970
And then, I was from
Westminster, California

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:37.803
and my grandma,

00:01:37.803 --> 00:01:39.310
she knew the people that owned

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:40.440
all the Edwards theaters.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.530
So I'd be over there too.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.730
I'm in Newport Beach, LA.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.053
So that's, those are the two places I grew

00:01:47.053 --> 00:01:48.052
up.

00:01:48.052 --> 00:01:51.040
- [Mark] Okay. And how long
have you been down here,

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:51.940
on skid row?

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.167
- About two months...three months.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:55.580
- [Mark] You're brand new.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.893
Right now, I'm, uh,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.160
It's just saving the world right now.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.470
- [Mark] You're saving the world?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.303
Yes, sir.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.233
- [Mark] Um...

00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:08.470
- I mean, opening keys that

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.200
I never knew I had the ability to

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.373
but when I had the ability
and God gave me that gift,

00:02:14.373 --> 00:02:16.543
then I started doing it.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.223
And special intelligence.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.470
And I'm a fan- a federal judge as well.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.303
- [Mark] You are?

00:02:24.303 --> 00:02:25.136
- Yes, sir.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.250
- [Mark] What's your,
what's your drug, Ruby?

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.404
- I, I, I do whatever everybody else does

00:02:33.404 --> 00:02:35.217
- [Mark] (laughing)
Well, that's everything.

00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:36.279
- Well, that's just whatever,

00:02:36.279 --> 00:02:38.373
I don't do heroin.
- [Mark] You don't do heroin?

00:02:38.373 --> 00:02:39.225
- No, sir.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.883
- [Mark] Got it. And
what do you do for money?

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.790
- Well, my husband collects
my welfare check right now.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.373
Not my welfare, my, my,

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.500
I lived in the hospital

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.110
when I was a child - all my life.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.210
I stayed in St. Joseph hospital.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.903
CHOC. Children's Hospital of Orange...

00:02:58.903 --> 00:02:59.736
- [Mark] So, you weren't with your family?

00:02:59.736 --> 00:03:00.770
- [Ruby] A lot. Yes, I was.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.180
My family, they'd come in and out

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.610
but I was like five years old

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.690
and I was always in -
living in the hospital.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.523
- [Mark] Why is that?

00:03:06.523 --> 00:03:08.280
- [Ruby] Because I had asthma.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.694
Chronic, chronic asthma, where
I almost died like two times.

00:03:11.694 --> 00:03:12.527
- [Mark] Wow.

00:03:12.527 --> 00:03:13.900
- [Ruby] Yes, severe asthma all the time

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.810
I was in the living at the hospital.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.360
So I'd be in and out of school.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.370
Was raised with real good family.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.020
So then I moved to
Apple Valley, California

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:28.680
and I married my, um

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.313
I divorced my husband.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.673
Legally separated because
he's very abusive.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.430
He sleep, uh, cheating on me
with other women downstairs,

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.706
so I had to get rid of him.

00:03:42.706 --> 00:03:46.763
And so then I lived with
my mother in the backyard.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.950
Well, one day the police,
they came, they arrested me

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.750
for throwing a pumpkin
at my dad and my stepdad.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.920
And my mother was very sick.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.600
She (mumbles) her mouth was open.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.780
They said she had cancer.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:05.283
Well, now that I found out my
husband was putting heroin.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.760
He was pumping heroin in
to keep us sedated alone.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:13.250
But I didn't know this at the time.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:17.640
And when I left there, they
said my mother was gone

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:18.653
that she had died.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:20.980
I don't believe that.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:23.074
Cause I seen her after that.

00:04:23.074 --> 00:04:26.847
In a Uhaul truck about
a year and a half ago.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.640
And, um, my children, they
went into foster care.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:35.463
- [Mark] How many children do you have?

00:04:35.463 --> 00:04:36.533
- I have five.

00:04:38.242 --> 00:04:39.840
- [Mark] Did you, did you raise them?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.460
- Yes. As much as I did,

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.293
- [Mark] And they were...

00:04:43.293 --> 00:04:44.630
- They were five.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.720
And my other one was of age.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.107
And I have a 13 year old right now.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.923
So, um,

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.390
they told me that she died

00:05:00.704 --> 00:05:01.920
and she didn't.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:02.753
So,

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.380
I believe that the people of America

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.570
are taking care of her underground.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:14.063
Cause I left a lot of people
underneath these, these floors.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:20.230
I've probably already let over

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.737
a trillion people out, I'd say.

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:26.502
Yes, sir.

00:05:26.502 --> 00:05:27.950
- [Mark] Where do you
sleep at night, Ruby?

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.543
- I sleep out just anywhere.

00:05:30.806 --> 00:05:32.060
- [Mark] Just on the street?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.220
- Yes, sir.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.652
- [Mark] No tent or anything like that?

00:05:34.652 --> 00:05:35.485
- Huh?

00:05:35.485 --> 00:05:36.710
- [Mark] No tent or anything like that.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.543
- I'm sorry.

00:05:37.543 --> 00:05:38.560
- [Mark] No tent?

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:42.700
- No. I sleep in different tents, stuff.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.250
Just whatever happens, happens.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.540
- [Mark] Have you ever been treated

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.307
for mental illness or anything like that?

00:05:51.307 --> 00:05:52.409
- I don't have a mental illness.

00:05:52.409 --> 00:05:53.242
- [Mark] You don't?

00:05:53.242 --> 00:05:54.075
- No.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:58.987
I live a very hard life,
but I'm the target.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.213
- [Mark] You're what?

00:06:02.213 --> 00:06:03.046
I'm the target.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.340
- [Mark] You're the target?

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.173
- Yes, sir.

00:06:06.173 --> 00:06:07.006
- [Mark] Of who?

00:06:07.006 --> 00:06:09.940
- Of rat playing games,

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.683
snake playing games,

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.094
spaceship, monsters,

00:06:15.094 --> 00:06:16.100
(laughs)

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.163
stuff like that.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.780
But I'm okay, and I'm alive

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.310
thanks to Jesus Christ.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.608
- [Mark] Is there one particular
drug that you lean on more?

00:06:25.608 --> 00:06:27.363
It doesn't matter if I do.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.940
I'm clear minded. I
understand what's going on.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.553
I feel it. I live it. I breathe it.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.310
- [Mark] Alright. Well, Ruby,
thank you for talking to me.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.176
- Thank you, brother.

00:06:41.176 --> 00:06:42.009
- [Mark] It's very interesting.

00:06:42.009 --> 00:06:43.675
- Yes, sir.
- [Mark] Good luck out there.

00:06:43.675 --> 00:06:45.366
- God bless you. Thank you.

00:06:45.366 --> 00:06:48.199
(traffic passing)

